              },
              "hints": [
                {
                  "content": "Think about what happens when a natural resource is consumed at a rate faster than nature can replace it. What are the long-term consequences?",
                  "images": {},
                  "replace": false,
                  "widgets": {}
                },
                {
                  "content": "Groundwater is replenished when precipitation (rain and snow) seeps into the ground. However, this process, known as recharge, can be very slow, sometimes taking hundreds or even thousands of years for deep aquifers to fully refill.",
                  "images": {},
